The page title reads:

MOVEMENT
Practices for Nervous System Regulation

A standing silhouette glows at center with faint motion echoes behind it.

Four instruction panels read:

MOVE – Change posture or position.
MOBILIZE – Invite range and circulation.
STRETCH – Ease tension without forcing range.
RELEASE – Allow excess activation to discharge.

The effect band reads:
Regulates the nervous system, reduces stored tension, and restores embodied alignment.

The bottom declaration reads:
MOVE YOUR BODY, CALM YOUR MIND, FEEL AT HOME IN YOURSELF

